id: fusion-of-ki
name: Fusion of Ki
kind: state
# A Special State (the user's terminology): "You can only enter the Fusion of Ki State through the effects of the Energy
# Synchronize Special Maneuver" - entered by it alone (fusion-of-ki.mjs), never offered on the sheet.
specialState: true
description: >
  Two Linked Characters' energies combined: one Ki pool between them, the other's Attribute Scores feeding your Modifiers, and
  Combat Rolls 1(T) higher side by side.
text: >
  The Fusion of Ki is a state of being with a concept similar to Fusion, but instead of combining two Characters, only their
  energies are combined. Combining energies in such a manner is a last resort for most fighters, as it risks exhausting both
  combatants. This is a very powerful technique that eliminates the weakness of Fusion (the reduction of allied combatants) while
  benefiting from its increased power, albeit for a very limited time.

  You can only enter the Fusion of Ki State through the effects of the Energy Synchronize Special Maneuver.

  (1)-[Automatic/Fusion of Ki]: Add together the Maximum Ki Point Pool and current Ki Point Pool of both Linked Characters – these
  are now known as the Maximum Linked Ki points and Linked Ki Points respectively. Until you leave this State, both Linked
  Characters use the Maximum Linked Ki Points and Linked Ki Points for their Maximum Ki Point Pool and Ki Point Pool respectively.

  (2)-[Permanent, Automatic]: Upon leaving this State, halve the Linked Ki Points. The Ki Point Pool of both Linked Characters
  becomes equal to that number of Ki Points. Additionally, if either of the Linked Characters are in a Transformation, they must
  make a Stress Test. If they fail the Stress Test, they gain the Stress Exhaustion Combat Condition until the end of their next turn.

  (3)-[Passive]: Increase your Attribute Modifiers by 1/4 (rounded up) of the Attribute Scores of those same Attributes from your
  Linked Character.

  (4)-[Passive]: While you and your Linked Character are on adjacent Squares, increase your Combat Rolls by 1(T).

  (5)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you use the United Attack Maneuver in response to their Linked Character’s Attacking Maneuver,
  double the effects of Additional Power and Wager.

  (6)-[Triggered/Fusion of Ki]: If your Linked Character is in the God Ki Special State and you are not, enter the God Ki Special
  State while you are in the Fusion of Ki State.

---

# Entered for 3 Combat Rounds, the Round it is entered in the first - as Limited's Rounds count (the user's) - or till the Linked
# Ki Points reach 0; left any other way too (Defeat, Stress Exhaustion, by hand), both leave it. All of it carried out by the GM,
# who may change both Characters (fusion-of-ki.mjs).
# (1) Both Pools summed as it is entered and kept on each (flag fusionOfKi): the Maximum read off it (actor-character.mjs), every
#     change to one's Ki Points written on the other's.
# (2) Left: half of the Linked Ki Points (rounded down) each. The Stress Test of one in a Transformation: said on its card -
#     Transformations are not in this system yet.
# (3) 1/4 of the Linked Character's Scores, rounded up, on your Modifiers - read off them (registry.mjs kiFusionPrograms).
# (5) In the United Attack window: a box, once a Combat Round (united-attack.mjs).
# (6) Automatic: entered with it, left with it.

[passive]
# (4) On a Square adjacent to your Linked Character's - read again as a token moves.
if (besideKiLink) {
    combatRolls += 1(T);
}
